            <ArticleTitle>Piezogenic pedal papules in two family members.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>260-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Piezogenic pedal papules are small, occasionally painful, fat herniations that become apparent when weight is placed on the heel. Although the cause is unknown, hereditary factors may play a role. This is the second report of two family members with this condition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
